./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:14:The label is not part of the anchor. A descriptive label such as `[validated by]` is never touched ([validated by: leaves a descriptive label alone while syncing a short-form one beside it](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L420)). A short-form `[Lnn](../../src/X.test.ts#Lnn)` is different: its label carries no meaning beyond the number, so it is force-synced to whatever its own href says ([validated by: syncs labels even in a spec skipped for a differing anchor set](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L399)). Syncing happens after the rewrite, so a repointed href carries its label with it in the same run ([validated by: carries the label along when the href is repointed](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L354)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:20:- That is what makes a second run against the same baseline a no-op rather than a second translation ([validated by: is a no-op the second time, because the baseline is read from the base ref](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L76)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:21:- `base-ref` defaults to `origin/main` ([validated by: defaults the base ref to origin/main](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L612)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:25:- A spec absent from the base ref is skipped whole. It is new, so no earlier line numbers exist to translate ([validated by: skips a spec absent from the base ref](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L234)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:26:- A spec whose ordered list of cited paths differs from the base ref's is skipped whole. Its anchors were authored against the working tree ([validated by: skips a spec whose ordered anchor paths differ from the base ref](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L214)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:27:- A single anchor whose line differs from the base spec's at the same position was deliberately retargeted by a spec edit. It is taken as authored, never rewritten, and counted under `retargeted (not checked)` ([validated by: takes a manually retargeted anchor as authored and never rewrites it](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L246)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:29:Skipping suspends only the baseline comparison. Rotten anchors are still reported in every one of those cases ([validated by: still checks a spec that was skipped for a differing anchor set](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L326)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:35:- Exactly one match is the answer ([validated by: moves each anchor to where the base ref's line content now lives](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L64)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:36:- Lines are compared with quotes and whitespace dropped, so a formatter pass over a cited file is not drift: the anchor follows the line it cited, and a file reformatted in place reads as up to date ([validated by: follows a line a formatter rewrote, because quotes and spacing are not drift](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L651), [validated by: reads a file reformatted in place as up to date under --check](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L664)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:37:- No match is `unresolved`: the cited line is gone, and a person has to decide what the spec meant ([validated by: reports an anchor whose baseline content is gone as unresolved, and leaves it alone](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L90)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:38:- Several matches are scored against the four lines either side, and the candidate whose neighbourhood best reproduces the baseline's wins ([validated by: picks the occurrence whose surrounding lines match the baseline](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L144)).
./specs/hal-engine-spec-anchor-drift/spec.md:39:- If two candidates score equally the anchor is `unresolved` as ambiguous. It is never a coin flip ([validated by: refuses to guess when the context ties, and rewrites nothing](../../scripts/repoint-spec-anchors.test.ts#L193)).
